WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.105
The federal requirement, from NIST special
publication eight hundred fifty-three,

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.475
revision five, as the guide's
requirements table maps it.

3
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:14.250
Step 9 supports C M two, baseline
configuration, C M six, configuration settings,

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.916
and C A seven, continuous monitoring;

5
00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:22.425
its evidence is the monthly compliance
export and the exemption register.

6
00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:28.456
Step 10 supports I R four, incident
handling, C P four, contingency plan testing,

7
00:00:28.456 --> 00:00:33.545
and A U six, audit record review;
its evidence is the review records,

8
00:00:33.545 --> 00:00:36.937
the exercises, and the
after-action reports.

9
00:00:36.937 --> 00:00:40.592
The guide notes that those controls
ask for incident handling,

10
00:00:40.592 --> 00:00:44.457
contingency plan testing and
continuous monitoring at Moderate,

11
00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:46.776
and that the cadence is the program's own.

12
00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:49.510
Each row lines up with the fed-ramp twenty

13
00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.325
X key security indicators the guide names.

14
00:00:52.325 --> 00:00:57.550
The steps support these controls; the
assessor decides whether each is satisfied.
